  "illustration_prompt": "Create a single publication-quality landscape 3:2 narrative illustration for an adult illustrated English-reading booklet. Finished standalone artwork, not a book mockup, not a collage of multiple unrelated panels. Sophisticated contemporary editorial gouache and watercolor, carefully controlled colored-pencil accents, velvety matte paint, subtle warm paper texture, soft natural daylight. Warm ivory paper dominates; subdued eucalyptus and sage greens structure the composition; restrained buttery lemon-yellow and dusty terracotta accents. Calm, comfortable, refined, credible drawing and natural anatomy. An airy coherent composition with one clear story focal point and at most two supporting details, generous breathing room at all edges and softly feathered painted edges into ivory. Detailed but uncluttered. Historically and scientifically appropriate objects, clothing and setting. Show the particular article's pivotal event or mechanism rather than a generic portrait or generic textbook symbols. Human figures treated with dignity; no grotesque caricature, no sensational violence or visible injuries. For disasters, emphasize the setting, evidence or human response without graphic suffering. For uncertain scientific claims, depict the observations and investigation without presenting debated mechanisms as proven. Absolutely no typography, captions, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, diagram labels, fake writing or invented charts anywhere. Do not render invisible forces as literal magic. Avoid corporate vector icons, slick 3D rendering and childish cartoon style. High-quality, print-ready visual storytelling, matching a warm ivory-and-sage adult watercolor booklet.\n\nARTICLE-SPECIFIC SCENE: Tu Youyou and one colleague at a modest Chinese research laboratory bench around 1971, thoughtfully examining sweet-wormwood leaves and a small unheated glass extraction flask containing pale herbal liquid. A neatly gathered sprig of Artemisia annua with fine divided leaves lies beside the flask. A second supporting detail is an old stitched Chinese medical handbook lying open but with absolutely blank, unlettered pages, suggesting a historical clue without fabricated writing. Tu wears a plain period pale lab coat, practical short dark hair, dignified calm concentration. Focal story is low-temperature extraction inspired by a method without boiling: no flame, no hot plate, no steaming pot, no triumphant miracle cure, no patients or self-dosing. Credible simple laboratory glassware with stoppered ether flask; no visible chemical labels or numbers. Ivory-and-sage editorial painting, not a generic scientist portrait.",
